WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.030 --> 00:00:04.590
The vision of kids is rapidly growing when&nbsp;
they are young. And once they reach 6,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:04.590 --> 00:00:09.660
it's completely developed. However, one&nbsp;
in five children have a vision disorder.

00:00:09.660 --> 00:00:17.580
Because children don’t know better, to them their&nbsp;
vision seems normal. Where one kid sees an eight,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:17.580 --> 00:00:22.590
the other might see a three. Too often,&nbsp;
teachers and adults also don’t know the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:22.590 --> 00:00:28.350
signs of a child’s impaired sight and wrongly&nbsp;
label them as slow or learning disabled.

00:00:28.350 --> 00:00:36.390
That’s why all kids should have a professional&nbsp;
eye check every one to two years. If that cannot&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:36.390 --> 00:00:41.100
be provided, it’s important for parents and&nbsp;
teachers to learn how to detect the condition.

00:00:41.100 --> 00:00:48.360
Here are some signs to spot eye problems.&nbsp;
A student asks to change seats from back&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:48.360 --> 00:00:53.610
to front. They look into their peers’ notebook&nbsp;
instead of the board. They squint their eyes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:53.610 --> 00:00:59.880
to focus on objects in the distance. They&nbsp;
look at things really close up. They execute&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:59.880 --> 00:01:04.830
handiwork poorly and their handwriting&nbsp;
is extraordinarily bad. Sometimes kids&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:04.830 --> 00:01:10.410
even walk clumsily. Or show some more explicit&nbsp;
symptoms like tearing or itching of the eyes.

00:01:10.410 --> 00:01:17.430
To perform a simple eye test, have your&nbsp;
student close one eye and read out loud&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:17.430 --> 00:01:24.030
a standard Tumbling E Chart from six meters away.&nbsp;
School children age 6 or above should be able to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:24.030 --> 00:01:29.400
read all lines including the one labeled&nbsp;
2030. Then repeat it with the other eye.

00:01:29.400 --> 00:01:36.480
When they do the test, observe the students’&nbsp;
posture and behavior. They shouldn’t have&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:36.480 --> 00:01:41.310
to move or tilt their head, turn their eyes&nbsp;
or constantly blink just to read the chart.

00:01:41.310 --> 00:01:48.660
If you identify a child with an eye problem,&nbsp;
please inform the parents. And if available,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:48.660 --> 00:01:53.520
the school’s doctor or principal. It’s&nbsp;
important to care early and to help kids&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:53.520 --> 00:01:58.590
learn and live better, and to prevent&nbsp;
further eye diseases. After the kid has&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:58.590 --> 00:02:03.540
received proper care by an eye specialist,&nbsp;
you might see a massive study improvement.

